   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 987 of the laws of 1971 amending the education law and\nthe civil practice law and rules relating to the regulation and practice of\ncertain professions; and to continue the dental society of the state of New\nYork, in relation to membership in the New York state dental association",
    "basePrintNo": "S7930",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7930-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§5 & 6, Chap 987 of 1971",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7930\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 987 of the laws of 1971 amend-\ning the education law and the civil practice law and rules relating to\nthe regulation and practice of certain professions; and to continue the\ndental society of the state of New York, in relation to membership in\nthe New York state dental association\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo conform the membership requirements of the New York State Dental\nAssociation and its local district and county dental societies to the\nrequirements of the American Dental Association.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 conforms the membership requirements of the New York State\nDental Association to those of the American Dental Association.\n\nSection 2 conforms the membership requirements of the district and coun-\nty dental societies of the New York State Dental Association to those of\nthe American Dental Association.\n\nSection 3 makes the bill effective immediately upon enactment.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York State Dental Association and its local district and county\ndental societies are all part of a three way contractual agreement with\nthe American Dental Association that requires all three levels to have\nconsistent bylaws and membership requirements.  The American Dental\nAssociation has altered its bylaws to allow membership for persons who\npossess dental degrees that qualify them for licensure even if they are\nnot licensed as dentists. The governing statute of the New York State\nDental Association limits membership to licensed dentists. If the New\nYork State Dental Association does not conform its membership require-\nments to those of the American Dental Association, it is subject to\nbeing expelled from the joint contract with the American Dental Associ-\nation - a devastating result for New York. Therefore, the change to the\ngoverning statute of the New York State Dental Association and its local\ndistrict and county dental societies is necessary to preserve the three\nway joint contract with the American Dental Association and to make\neligible for membership persons with dental degrees that would qualify\nthem for licensure, even though not licensed as dentists. This category\nprimarily covers dental researchers, public health dentists, dental\nschool faculty members and those few others who may obtain licensure\nqualifying dental degrees but who choose not to get a dental license.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
